Sure! Here’s a quick example of how you can call the `requests_get` function to pull the latest annual income statement for Apple (AAPL). Just replace the placeholder `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual key:

```json
{
  "name": "requests_get",
  "arguments": {
    "url": "https://financialmodelingprep.com/api/v3/income-statement",
    "params": {
      "symbol": "AAPL",
      "period": "annual",
      "datatype": "json",
      "limit": 5
    },
    "apikey": "YOUR_API_KEY"
  }
}
```

If you’d like data for a different company or a specific CIK, just let me know the symbol or CIK and any other preferences (e.g., quarterly data, CSV format, etc.) and I’ll craft the exact call for you.
